codex
Root cause is now concrete: the audit container’s `getpid()` reports its PID-namespace value, while `/proc` is mounted from a different namespace, so Lean’s `/proc/<pid>/exe` lookup returns `ENOENT`. A minimal audit-only preload shim can make that lookup use the equivalent `/proc/self/exe`; it affects installation discovery only, not parsing, elaboration, compilation, or kernel checking. I’m preserving the shim source and diagnosis, then rerunning the trusted preflight with this environment correction.
apply patch
